00:55:31.101 --> 00:55:32.550
your perspectives on that,

00:55:32.550 --> 00:55:35.922
and what you see as the improvements,

00:55:35.922 --> 00:55:38.842
or what that all will
mean for us as a country

00:55:38.842 --> 00:55:41.940
trying to move forward on so
many of these important topics?

00:55:41.940 --> 00:55:45.210
- Well, as you know our
criminal justice system

00:55:45.210 --> 00:55:48.630
has been the default for a
lack of a mental health system,

00:55:48.630 --> 00:55:49.950
and addiction treatment system.

00:55:49.950 --> 00:55:53.310
So we end up incarcerating people

00:55:53.310 --> 00:55:55.530
because we don't give
them the interventions

00:55:55.530 --> 00:55:58.470
for their mental illness or addiction.

00:55:58.470 --> 00:56:01.470
And as you know we incarcerate

00:56:01.470 --> 00:56:03.390
a greater percentage of our population

00:56:03.390 --> 00:56:07.080
than any other free industrialized
nation in the world.

00:56:07.080 --> 00:56:10.461
So the indictment is actually
on our justice system

00:56:10.461 --> 00:56:15.461
that it's not working,
it's not keeping us safe.

00:56:15.859 --> 00:56:20.859
There is 75% recidivism from
state prison within five years,

00:56:21.690 --> 00:56:24.030
50% within two years.

00:56:24.030 --> 00:56:27.690
A majority of violent crimes
are committed by people

00:56:27.690 --> 00:56:28.890
who've already been in prison.

00:56:28.890 --> 00:56:32.250
Like, we should just look
at this thing and think of,

00:56:32.250 --> 00:56:34.620
well, where do we want incarceration?

00:56:34.620 --> 00:56:37.800
We want incarceration to protect us,

00:56:37.800 --> 00:56:39.840
but outside of that, what do we want?

00:56:39.840 --> 00:56:41.880
We wanna be making sure

00:56:41.880 --> 00:56:44.700
that we treat people with mental illness.

00:56:44.700 --> 00:56:46.638
We treat people with addiction.

00:56:46.638 --> 00:56:51.360
In the 988 we're in the first opportunity

00:56:51.360 --> 00:56:54.930
to really seek fundamental
reform in this paradigm

00:56:54.930 --> 00:56:58.051
because instead of the
police officers showing up,

00:56:58.051 --> 00:57:01.050
which as I mentioned earlier,

00:57:01.050 --> 00:57:03.840
if you have a mental illness,
or you're a person of color,

00:57:03.840 --> 00:57:05.739
you're more likely to be shot,

00:57:05.739 --> 00:57:09.360
and have a much, obviously, poor response.

00:57:09.360 --> 00:57:13.059
Let's think about how this 988

00:57:13.059 --> 00:57:16.821
you could have in communities of color,

00:57:16.821 --> 00:57:20.190
someone show up that
looks like the community

00:57:20.190 --> 00:57:21.750
they're coming from.

00:57:21.750 --> 00:57:23.130
You could have someone show up

00:57:23.130 --> 00:57:25.860
who's not only someone
looks like the community,

00:57:25.860 --> 00:57:28.830
but knows the situations

00:57:28.830 --> 00:57:30.870
in terms of if it's a
person with mental illness,

00:57:30.870 --> 00:57:32.793
knows how to deescalate.

00:57:34.290 --> 00:57:38.700
And provide the right
intervention so that, one,

00:57:38.700 --> 00:57:40.830
they don't get a criminal record,

00:57:40.830 --> 00:57:42.840
and, therefore, they're able to recover

00:57:42.840 --> 00:57:46.440
because it's easier to recover
if you can still get a job,

00:57:46.440 --> 00:57:48.270
'cause you don't have this conviction

00:57:48.270 --> 00:57:49.800
sitting over your head.

00:57:49.800 --> 00:57:54.030
Wouldn't it be great to get
pre-adjudication in all of that?

00:57:54.030 --> 00:57:56.250
And by the way, some of
these service courts,

00:57:56.250 --> 00:57:59.760
like mental health courts,
drug courts, and the like,

00:57:59.760 --> 00:58:03.090
are already showing the value of this.

00:58:03.090 --> 00:58:05.760
In Rhode Island, I was
really proud to be part of

00:58:05.760 --> 00:58:07.560
expanding the Veterans Court.

00:58:07.560 --> 00:58:11.220
So in the wake of Iraq and Afghanistan,

00:58:11.220 --> 00:58:14.040
we had the second highest percentage

00:58:14.040 --> 00:58:19.040
of our Guard and Reserve war
police units, military police.

00:58:19.440 --> 00:58:21.270
And they all came from Rhode Island's

00:58:21.270 --> 00:58:26.130
municipal police academies
and organizations.

00:58:26.130 --> 00:58:27.780
And what happened was

00:58:27.780 --> 00:58:29.880
when they came back from
Iraq and Afghanistan,

00:58:29.880 --> 00:58:32.400
they found themselves
showing up at incidences

00:58:32.400 --> 00:58:36.720
where they were arresting
the very fellow officers

00:58:36.720 --> 00:58:40.560
they had just served in Afghanistan with,

00:58:40.560 --> 00:58:43.770
and in Iraq with who were suffering from

00:58:43.770 --> 00:58:48.720
the untreated impact of
post-traumatic stress.

00:58:48.720 --> 00:58:52.478
And so, of course, it was
bothering them this was happening.

00:58:52.478 --> 00:58:57.000
And why should we be locking
up one of our freedom fighters,

00:58:57.000 --> 00:58:58.830
one of our Veterans,

00:58:58.830 --> 00:59:01.290
because we didn't adequately
take care of their,

00:59:01.290 --> 00:59:03.060
quote, invisible wounds of war,

00:59:03.060 --> 00:59:05.940
but, frankly, as you
know our response to the,

00:59:05.940 --> 00:59:07.290
quote, invisible wounds of war

00:59:07.290 --> 00:59:09.600
has been invisible in many respects.

00:59:09.600 --> 00:59:11.700
We've tried to ramp up in the years past,

00:59:11.700 --> 00:59:13.893
but we've been playing catch up

00:59:13.893 --> 00:59:18.060
with 22 Veterans dying each
day at their own hands.

00:59:18.060 --> 00:59:20.280
So my point is,

00:59:20.280 --> 00:59:24.630
is that we need a different
emergency response.

00:59:24.630 --> 00:59:27.930
And if we have a different response,

00:59:27.930 --> 00:59:31.020
we'd get different outcomes down the line.

00:59:31.020 --> 00:59:33.750
So why not try to train that up?

00:59:33.750 --> 00:59:34.620
Now to do this,

00:59:34.620 --> 00:59:37.680
you have to build out a
whole continuum of care,

00:59:37.680 --> 00:59:39.030
which as I mentioned earlier,

00:59:39.030 --> 00:59:41.160
we've so underfunded mental
health all these years,

00:59:41.160 --> 00:59:44.670
we don't have an infrastructure
to meet this need.

00:59:44.670 --> 00:59:46.770
988, in my view, Dr. Addy,

00:59:46.770 --> 00:59:49.470
is gonna show the pitfalls
of our current system

00:59:49.470 --> 00:59:53.460
as being inadequate because
when we stand this up,

00:59:53.460 --> 00:59:56.760
everyone expects the
number of crisis calls

00:59:56.760 --> 01:00:01.760
to minimally quadruple
just grow exponentially.

01:00:02.340 --> 01:00:04.110
And we don't even have the capacity

01:00:04.110 --> 01:00:06.510
to meet our current needs,

01:00:06.510 --> 01:00:10.230
let alone inviting people
to use a three digit number,

01:00:10.230 --> 01:00:12.120
and supposed to 911

01:00:12.120 --> 01:00:15.360
to call for a mental
health crisis response.

01:00:15.360 --> 01:00:18.210
And I just think the
thing's gonna fall down,

01:00:18.210 --> 01:00:19.710
and implode on itself.

01:00:19.710 --> 01:00:23.820
And then, hopefully, that
will spur us into action.

01:00:23.820 --> 01:00:25.230
And we'll say, oh my God,

01:00:25.230 --> 01:00:26.880
we were a little premature on this,

01:00:26.880 --> 01:00:30.270
or maybe we didn't get ourselves
organized for it enough.

01:00:30.270 --> 01:00:34.503
And we'll do what we need
to do to follow that up, so.

01:00:36.660 --> 01:00:37.980
988, it's a big deal.

01:00:37.980 --> 01:00:40.890
Honestly, there's very
little understanding of it

01:00:40.890 --> 01:00:45.890
amongst the local, county,
municipal level officials

01:00:48.060 --> 01:00:51.810
that are gonna be necessary
to put this into effect.

01:00:51.810 --> 01:00:55.710
And so if they don't understand
it, and if by the way,

01:00:55.710 --> 01:00:58.830
there's no kind of really
good technical assistance,

01:00:58.830 --> 01:01:01.410
and how-to then what kind of system?

01:01:01.410 --> 01:01:04.440
Because, by the way, it's gonna
change from locale to locale

01:01:04.440 --> 01:01:08.190
because some systems are
gonna have really good

01:01:08.190 --> 01:01:09.840
kind of maybe urgent care,

01:01:09.840 --> 01:01:11.869
or really good the right number of people

01:01:11.869 --> 01:01:14.190
to answer the phone,

01:01:14.190 --> 01:01:17.670
but what about the people to
show up to help that person

01:01:17.670 --> 01:01:18.810
are there enough of those people?

01:01:18.810 --> 01:01:21.000
And what about the places to go?

01:01:21.000 --> 01:01:22.620
So if you got a person answering the call,

01:01:22.620 --> 01:01:23.970
then you need someone to show up,

01:01:23.970 --> 01:01:25.200
then you need a place to go.

01:01:25.200 --> 01:01:29.352
Like, we need, like, the whole continuum.

01:01:29.352 --> 01:01:31.620
And different places in the country

01:01:31.620 --> 01:01:33.873
have different aspects of that continuum.

01:01:36.330 --> 01:01:39.060
It's gonna be a while
before we do this right,

01:01:39.060 --> 01:01:43.800
